1. ANDROID 12 -> 17 RULES (apply in every module)
- Version-aware code: one Compat layer; branch only where 31 / 33 / 34 / 35 / 36 / 37 differ. Before each module read the official behaviour-change pages for Android 12 to 17 (including QPR releases) and apply them.
- Manifest hygiene: explicit android:exported; PendingIntent FLAG_IMMUTABLE / FLAG_MUTABLE; foregroundServiceType + the matching FOREGROUND_SERVICE_* permission (34+); POST_NOTIFICATIONS (33+); NEARBY_WIFI_DEVICES (33+) or fine location for Wi-Fi scans; BLUETOOTH_CONNECT / BLUETOOTH_SCAN (31+); READ_MEDIA_* and partial photo access (33/34+); exact-alarm permissions; USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT is restricted on 34+ (guard it, provide a fallback).
- ALWAYS-ON ENGINE RULE (most important). A microphone foreground service started from the background gets no microphone data (Android 12-13) or fails with a SecurityException (Android 14+), even when started from BOOT_COMPLETED; it also needs RECORD_AUDIO at creation. It can legitimately be started from a visible activity, a notification action tap, a home-screen widget tap, or by the app that provides the VoiceInteractionService. Therefore: (1) in onboarding make the app the DEFAULT DIGITAL ASSISTANT (RoleManager ROLE_ASSISTANT) with a VoiceInteractionService + session service (plus any RecognitionService the platform needs to list the app as selectable - verify) and start/restart the microphone engine from that service, including after reboot; (2) if I decline the role: start the engine while the app is visible, or from a one-tap "Wake" notification action or widget, and after a reboot post that one-tap notification instead of failing silently; (3) never start the engine from a BOOT_COMPLETED receiver.
- ANDROID 17 BACKGROUND-AUDIO HARDENING: speech playback, audio-focus requests and volume / ringer changes from the background only work inside a foreground service that has while-in-use capability (a service started at boot is silenced). Keep the whole audio path inside the always-on engine; detect silent suppression (AUDIOFOCUS_REQUEST_FAILED, zero output level, volume or ringer value unchanged after a set) and warn me with a notification; read back every volume / ringer change to verify it.
- Microphone privacy (12+): the system shows a mic indicator whenever we listen (cannot be hidden) and I can switch the mic off system-wide: detect all-zero audio and tell me.
- Clipboard (12+) shows a read toast: never read the clipboard; if pasting a password is the only fallback, mark it sensitive and clear it immediately.
- Background activity launches are restricted and were hardened again in Android 15 and 17: never assume startActivity from the background works. Use the strongest legitimate route (visible overlay window with SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW - on 15+ it must be visible -, assistant session, notification / full-screen intent, Accessibility) and VERIFY that the target app or screen really came to the front.
